// Accepted deviations from SonarQube Cloud's findings.
//
// This is the one place a Sonar finding is argued with. A fix session that thinks a finding
// is wrong adds an entry here with a reason; it does not add // NOSONAR comments, #[allow]
// attributes, or turn a rule off. See docs/adr/0017-sonar-backlog-becomes-batched-github-issues.md.
//
// Entry shape:
//   rule     required. The full Sonar rule key, e.g. "rust:S3776".
//   verdict  "fix" (default), "accept" (never file it), or "defer" (not now).
//   paths    optional globs narrowing the entry. "**" crosses directories, "*" does not.
//   message  optional regex the finding's message must match.
//   reason   required for accept and defer. A reason appealing to a repo-wide design
//            choice must cite an ADR or a ticket, so review can check it.
//
// Example:
//   {
//     "rule": "rust:S3776",
//     "verdict": "accept",
//     "paths": ["crates/core/src/turn.rs"],
//     "reason": "Why this rule is wrong *here*, citing an ADR or a ticket."
//   }
//
// A verdict of accept or defer without a reason is a hard error: that is how a backlog
// quietly rots. Nothing here is hidden - every run prints the suppressed count by rule.
{
  "rules": [
    {
      "rule": "javascript:S3504",
      "verdict": "accept",
      "paths": ["crates/cli/web/quad-storage.js"],
      "reason": "Vendored upstream quad-storage 0.1.3, kept as vendored and re-vendored with the crate (ADR-0037, ticket 3066; crates/cli/web/README.md); its one local patch is the plugin version. Its top-level vars are page globals shared across classic scripts: sapp_jsutils.js, loaded just before, also declares `var ctx`, so `let ctx` here would throw a SyntaxError and the storage plugin would never load. Ticket 3033 (parked) replaces the file with the engine's own plugin."
    },
    {
      "rule": "javascript:S2703",
      "verdict": "accept",
      "paths": ["crates/cli/web/quad-storage.js"],
      "reason": "Vendored upstream quad-storage 0.1.3, kept as vendored and re-vendored with the crate (ADR-0037, ticket 3066; crates/cli/web/README.md); its one local patch is the plugin version, and another would have to be reapplied at every re-vendor. Ticket 3033 (parked) replaces the file with the engine's own plugin."
    }
  ]
}
